# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries and compiled outputs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/
dist/

# `go build ./...` inside a command directory writes the binary
# beside its source. Ignored by path because the name carries no
# extension to match on; it was committed twice before this.
cmd/eidos-reference/eidos-reference
bench/
.ergon/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage outputs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
fuzz/
.eidos/
.eidos-reference/

# Rapid failfiles under testdata/rapid/ are committed for auto-replay
# regression. Only ignore rapid/ at the repo root (build artifacts).
!/testdata/rapid/
!**/testdata/rapid/

# Fuzz corpora under testdata/fuzz/ are committed for the same reason:
# `go test -fuzz` writes each input it finds to
# testdata/fuzz/<Target>/<hash>, and committing it replays that input as
# an ordinary unit test on every subsequent run, forever. The bare
# `fuzz/` rule above matches those directories too, so without these
# every reproducer the fuzzer earns is discarded before it can be staged.
!/testdata/fuzz/
!**/testdata/fuzz/
coverage.txt
coverage.html
profile.out

